course: dictionary
lesson: 2468
title: Dart: a throw, an arrow, or a quick move
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Dart can be a thing you throw, or a fast movement. The words around it tell you which meaning fits. «Many reef fish have a false eye spot near the tail, so a hunter strikes at the wrong end while the fish darts away.» The fish is not throwing anything. It is moving suddenly and very quickly, so darts means moves fast.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. Swap in «moves suddenly and very quickly»: «while the fish moves suddenly and very quickly away» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Now try «throws a small object»: «while the fish throws a small object away» does not make sense, so that meaning is wrong here.
explain: Dart also names a game. «Play darts» means throwing small pointed objects at a round board, called a dartboard, and counting the scores. The same word can be a noun (a dart) or a verb (to dart). Check the small clues, like the words before and after it, to tell which one you are reading.
fact: Dart is a noun and a verb.
fact: As a noun, a dart is a small pointed object thrown at a round board in the game called darts, or a small sharp arrow, often blown or shot.
fact: As a verb, to dart means to move suddenly and very quickly.
fact: «Dart a look» is a phrase meaning to give a quick glance.
fact: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you are right.
exercise: «Many reef fish have a false eye spot near the tail, so a hunter strikes at the wrong end while the fish darts away.» What does darts mean here? | Sleeps under a rock | Shines brightly | *Moves suddenly and very quickly | Throws a small object at a board
exercise: Maya and Sam play darts at the pub on Friday night. What is a dart in this game? | *A small pointed object thrown at a round board | A long road through the hills | A kind of fish from the reef | A soft blanket
exercise: «Most vivid dreams happen in REM sleep, when the eyes dart about under the eyelids.» Find and copy one word from this sentence that means to move suddenly and quickly. | eyelids | dreams | *dart | vivid
test: Dad says, «Dart a look at the clock, Sam, we are late.» What does dart a look mean? | *To glance quickly | To close your eyes | To stare for an hour | To throw a look at a dartboard
test: Yesterday the rabbit ___ into the bushes when the dog barked. Which word fits the gap? | darting | darts | *darted | dart
exam: In «The small dart hit the board, and the mouse darted under the sofa», what is the meaning of dart in the first use? | *A small pointed object thrown at a board | A bright colour | A kind of fish | To move suddenly and very quickly
